      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As someone who locks and unlocks their gestures multiple times a minute while chatting with someone, the new gesture toggle feels very intrusive and yet also not obvious whether I've toggled it on or off at a glance. The icons within the notification are too small and similar to each other to easily distinguish between them, as is the text, so I'm having to pay closer attention to the notification to see which way I've toggled it. VS the old icons which were very obvious what the difference is at a glance. I shouldn't have to pay such close attention to the notification to see which way it was toggled.\nIf you're dead set on keeping the notification for it maybe change the colour of the notification box to be green when toggled on and grey when toggled off?\ntldr; the old HUD icons were much more clear and preferable to the new notifications for the gesture toggle",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-09-08T09:53:03.619Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Small little gripe with the new open beta, i'm not a fan of the popup for when you lock or unlock gestures, i lock mine constantly so the little popup is strange for 2 reasons. First is that I think its strange that it needs its own tab and text when the mic icon next to it still uses a standard icon. Secondly, it gets confusing to have to read the text to see if I just unlocked or locked my gestures after i've forgotten about them for a few minutes. I'd personally much rather see this reverted back to the old icon or at least given the option to switch to the icon! Thank you!",
